From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:51:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Align Auth for MCP, CIMD, and Agent as Principal flows with
 Auth0 docs and MCP spec

MCP server (resource server):
- PRM `resource` is the MCP server's public URL, which is also the Auth0 API
  identifier and the validated `aud`; drop non-PRM fields
- Remove the self-served /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server (Auth0
  publishes its own AS metadata)
- 401 responses carry WWW-Authenticate resource_metadata; 403 responses
  carry error="insufficient_scope" with the required scope
- Stop trusting the unauthenticated X-User-Token header; Token Vault now
  exchanges the validated bearer with the MCP server's own Custom API client,
  with an optional verified first-party fallback
- Log and surface caller identity (sub, client_id, act chain) per tool call

First-party agent:
- OBO client documented as a Custom API client linked to the Nexus Agent API;
  OBO requests only the called tool's scope; cache keyed on a token hash

Third-party agent (Acme):
- Onboarded by importing its CIMD URL (client_id = CIMD URL), with a reviewed
  read-only per-app grant, domain-level connection and its own Agent record
- Discovers via PRM and Auth0 metadata, requires PKCE S256, sends RFC 8707
  `resource`, checks RFC 9207 `iss`; runs on port 3003

Provisioning:
- Rename APIs to Nexus Agent API / Nexus MCP Server; per-app authorization
  and agent_subject_claims on the MCP server API
- Provision the MCP server's Custom API client with the Token Vault grant
- Enable resource parameter profile, iss parameter, and CIMD registration;
  promote the database connection to domain level

Verification, UI, lab guides, and READMEs updated to match.

